title The room nobody heard, put on a stopwatch
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; the card named the equinox family and named its first move -- a stopwatch before a roster row
think Cold roster opened 63 of 63 green in about fifty minutes, tree at 153a7fc22b21. Rota row by hand was 2 (Fire/Mars -- standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal); after the fast-forward N read 3462, so N mod 5 confirmed row 2 by arithmetic.
think Read the reach scan by family rather than by count. The `equinox` prefix reads 144, and the ROOM reads better: tools/gen/season/ holds 298 tracked witnesses and 3 are reached, so 295 stand unheard -- 24.6% of the tree's whole 1,201 unreached, in one directory.
think Ran the sequential sing and stopped it at a clean denominator. 47 of 144 cost 1,117,243 ms, per witness 178 ms to 204,250 ms, because 111 of 144 chain an elder and each rung re-runs the chain beneath it. A sing rung by rung is quadratic, so the sequential reading was never the one to finish.
think Switched to the leaves -- 33 witnesses that call scans and chain nobody. Two minutes for all of them, and every chained failure resolves to a leaf or a scan, so that is where a root lives. 16 green, 17 red at the open.
think Bisected the reds to one root wearing two coats. construction/REDS.md folds; row 42 has lived at archive/REDS-voice-season-rows-25-57.md since its fold; 19 sites across 17 scans grep the LIVING PIN for a numbered elder row, and 21 sites across 15 scans grep it for that row's lesson text on the line below.
think Fetched xykj61 before booking a row, which is the mitigation REDS %230 names. It had moved 6 commits ahead; their spine also ended at 230, so no collision, and the fast-forward was clean.
obs The fast-forward carried a red in with it. construction/ITINERARY.md arrived at 25,554 bytes and construction/SHRED_PREP.md at 24,620, both over the 24,576 each declares. Three leaves fell together -- e123 directly, then e125 and e126 whose scans call it as elder under `set -eu` and so died before printing a reason. My cold roster had read 63 green twenty minutes earlier against the tree before the merge. Booked as %232: a fast-forward is a tree change, and the green that opened the lap measured a different tree than the one it ships.
obs The merge carried a third refusal, and it is the sharpest: tools/l/launch-claude-season.rish prints the unattended recipe as a single-quoted prompt, and the new sync-rota clause added three lone apostrophes -- the round's own, upstream's, a module's witness map -- on both printed lines. A lone quote flips everything after it out of quoting, so both launch lines died on the next parenthesis. Six doubled; the scan reads 6 runnable lines, 0 that do not parse. REDS %211's fault, in the file that guard was written for, a day later.
obs My own hand-fold of rows %226-%229 moved ten relative links one directory deeper without deepening them -- REDS %183 exactly, in the room whose repair note says the REDS shelf holds no generator and its links are deepened by hand. readme_reach caught it on the hot pass, naming each broken link and its file. The loom fired, which is the system working.
obs Owned in my own hand: the first repoint pass read as a regression, 16 green to 14, and I checked before claiming. The three that moved were the merge's, not mine -- my repoint turned one leaf green and broke nothing.
obs Booking %231 and %232 pushed the living pin past its own bound, so rows %226-%229 folded to a shelf. The new spine reading then found %226 at its new home with no edit -- the guard earning itself on the lap it was written.
obs A witness must cite text that exists. My first spine-grep assertion quoted a lesson phrase from memory; the archive holds a shorter form, and the witness reds until the citation is real. Fixed before it left the working tree.
